    "message": "feat(analytics): name the vision model, and record an image with nowhere to go\n\nFollow-up to 5.13.0, from two questions: does a fallback *inside* the vision\nchain get tracked, and does the request say which vision model was used.\n\nThe chain was already tracked end to end -- verified against the real router\nand in the dashboard: a request whose vision model fails and whose vision\nfallback answers records the full three-hop chain, route_attempt=1, and\nroute_primary_model=<the vision model>, and renders as both a \"vision\" badge\nand a \"fallback 1, after chatgpt_oauth/gpt-5.6-luna\" badge. The failover panel\nshows the vision model's own failover; the diverted panel shows what each\ndiversion was ultimately served by. No change needed there.\n\nTwo real gaps, both now closed.\n\n**The vision model was only implied.** It is the head of the chain on a\ndiverted request, which you can only read off the trace if you already know\nhow diversion works. The detail now names it outright -- \"gpt-5.6-luna --\nanswered\", or \"gpt-5.6-luna -- failed, answered by <model>\".\n\n**An image with nowhere to go recorded nothing.** When a request carries an\nimage and no model on the route is known to accept one, the policy logs\nVISION ROUTE UNAVAILABLE and sends it anyway. The plan recorded no diversion,\nbecause nothing was replaced -- so the single case an operator most needs to\nsee was indistinguishable from an ordinary request. RouteDiversion gains\nVISION_UNAVAILABLE, recorded with route_diverted_from left NULL because\nnothing was in fact replaced.\n\nThat makes route_diversion no longer mean \"a diversion happened\", so both\ncounters now key on route_diverted_from, which is the field that actually\nmeans the head was replaced. The window stats gain vision_unavailable beside\nit: the safety net working and the safety net having nowhere to put the\nrequest are different facts and must not be summed.\n\nDashboard: a \"no vision route\" badge, a bordered note naming the fix\n(MODEL_VISION), an \"Image, no vision route\" figure, and a \"Vision model\" row.\n\nVerification:\n- probes of all four policy branches: adapter leads, adapter's own fallback\n  answers, no adapter but a sighted entry leads, and nothing sighted anywhere\n- browser on a throwaway home with all five row shapes: badges, the two\n  panels, the trace hops, and the new rows all correct; no console errors\n- both new colours measured composited over their real backgrounds in four\n  themes: badge 15.3-18.0:1, note 14.0-19.8:1. The first attempt used --warn\n  for the text, which measures 4.1:1 on the light theme -- under AA -- so warn\n  moved to the border and fill\n- full suite 3861 passed, 6 pre-existing PowerShell installer failures\n\nOne existing test seeded route_diversion without route_diverted_from, a shape\nthe router never writes; it now seeds both and pins that an unavailable row is\nnot counted as a diversion.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti",
